<http://data.silknow.org/object/7f6ac809-5272-3b1e-aa82-b59f38cff2a5/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Pocket case of tapestry woven silver filé and crimson silk floss in a pattern of fleur-de-lys and dolphins.  It is rectangular in shape with a triangular flap, reinforced with pasteboard and lined with pink silk taffeta. The seams and edges are couched with ¼-inch (4 mm) wide woven silver lace (braid).  There is a loop of silver filé cord at the point of the flap."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7f6ac809-5272-3b1e-aa82-b59f38cff2a5> .

